class.description:
[DisNetwork] owns one IPv4 UDP socket. Add it to the scene, set the connection properties and connect to its signals. With [member autostart] it opens the socket in [code]_ready[/code] and reads every waiting datagram each frame; the socket is never opened inside the editor. Each datagram is split into its PDUs (a datagram may bundle several), filtered by [member exercise_id] and by the sender's site/application, decoded, and emitted as [signal pdu_received] followed by a signal specific to the PDU type. Malformed or unsupported packets emit [signal packet_rejected] instead. Outgoing PDUs are encoded with [method send_pdu] or sent as raw bytes with [method send_bytes]. The node adds itself to the group [code]dis_network[/code], which [DisEntity], [DisEntityManager] and the other DIS nodes use to find it when no path is set. [codeblock] @onready var network: DisNetwork = $DisNetwork
func _ready() -> void: network.entity_state_received.connect(_on_entity_state)
func _on_entity_state(pdu: DisEntityStatePdu) -> void: print(pdu.marking, " at ", pdu.location_ecef) [/codeblock] [b]Note:[/b] Changing connection properties while running has no effect until [method start] is called again.
